## Windows build flags for plant.
##
## On macOS/Linux, plant's undefined XAD `Tape` symbols (from odelia's compiled
## ODE Solver) are resolved at *load* time against odelia's globally-loaded DLL
## (see odelia's `.onLoad` / odelia#28 and odelia's ARCHITECTURE.md), so the
## plain src/Makevars needs no odelia on the link line.
##
## Windows mingw `ld` forbids undefined symbols in a DLL, so that runtime trick
## cannot apply here: plant.dll must resolve odelia's `Tape` symbols at *link*
## time. We link directly against odelia's single compiled DLL (which exports
## the XAD Tape runtime), keeping one shared copy of `Tape`/`active_tape_` in the
## process. Tracked upstream in traitecoevo/odelia#29.

CXX_STD = CXX20

## ⚠️ THE SAME TWO DEFINES AS src/Makevars, AND THEY MATTER MORE HERE. odelia's
## active tape is a __thread variable whose storage class is not part of the
## mangled name, and Windows is the one platform where plant.dll resolves it at
## LINK time against odelia.dll rather than at load. A mismatch links cleanly,
## passes load, and corrupts every recorded derivative. Change one file and you
## must change all four. One assignment rather than two: appending to a variable
## in a second line is a GNU make extension R CMD check warns on.
PKG_CPPFLAGS = -isystem../inst/include/ -DXAD_NO_THREADLOCAL -DXAD_USE_STRONG_INLINE

## odelia's compiled DLL lives under its installed, arch-specific libs dir
## (.../odelia/libs/x64). Resolve the base libs dir in R, then append R's
## $(R_ARCH) make-variable (e.g. /x64) here -- doing the arch in make avoids the
## shell expanding `$r_arch` out of the Rscript expression.
ODELIA_LIBDIR = $(shell "${R_HOME}/bin/Rscript" -e "cat(system.file('libs', package='odelia'))")
PKG_LIBS = "$(ODELIA_LIBDIR)$(R_ARCH)/odelia.dll"

## Link to gperftools profiler
## Uncomment next line if you want to use the profiler.
## PKG_LIBS += -lprofiler
